uction is  huge matched only by admiration for the  firefighters  and worries for the future it's very  hard it's a lot of money we have to  spend  to make this from the beginning  you can't save anything  as you can see hundreds are yet to  return to vari bobby  extraordinary and devastating images  will greet them  and so too will the challenge of trying  to recover  back in turkey the lack of preparedness  has sparked much anger and criticism of  the country's leader  prompting a rash of social media  hashtags calling on other countries to  help  politics is never far away in turkey but  with about a quarter of the country  covered by forest  the nation's been particularly  vulnerable after droughts and record  temperatures  coupled with the lack of firefighting  aircraft  it's been a constant race against the  elements for exhausted firefighting  crews  and two in turkey have died whilst  others were dispatched from istanbul  around 700 kilometers away to boost the  battle force  the fires have ripped through thousands  of hectares of forest  turning trees and farmland into ash  and they aren't done yet  extra firefighters have been called in  to help in the battle along this aegean  coast  the beast of a fire is now heading  towards holiday homes  and a nearby power plant which provides  electricity  to more than half a million people  they're working day and night to cut  scars in the forest and create a fire  break to slow the flames down  bringing in heavy machinery to fell  trees and forge a path to save lives  homes and businesses  helicopters ferried buckets of ocean  water to dump on the flames  over and over again there's been a  visible increase in personnel here  as the fires rampage through  local residents watched aghast at the  unfurling emergency  one week on they're still struggling to  contain the fires  amid some of the highest temperatures on  record  and despite the constant ash raining  down some tourists  pressed on with their holidays a fe